<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34556" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pentăpŏlis</span></b> ,
		is, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πεντάπολις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A district of five towns on the Dead Sea</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sap.
				10, 6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A district of Cyrene</i>, <i>on the
				Libyan Sea</i>, Sex. <i><span class="en">Ruf. Brev.
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Verg. A. 4,
			42</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pentă-pŏlĭtānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Pentapolis</i>, i. e. <i>to Cyrene</i>, <i>Cyrenaic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 5, 5, § 31</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
